From eeaec82a9e4da41becf9cf6f47d4210aab2889e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:35:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: release the moved node's old document before
 post-connection steps

Node::insert blocks script on both the node's old document and the parent's
document, and queues the post-connection steps as a delayed task on the
parent's document. It released the parent's blocker first, which ran those
steps while the old document was still blocked. An iframe inserted from a
child frame fires `load` synchronously during its post-connection steps, and
when the listener came from the child's realm, call_setup found that realm's
document blocked and panicked ("DOM not in a stable state"). dailymotion.com
hit this on most loads.

Release the old document first, as Node::adopt already does, so the document
holding the delayed task is the last one released.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 components/script/dom/node/node.rs | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/script/dom/node/node.rs b/components/script/dom/node/node.rs
index 16c3aed821a..247083d278c 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/node/node.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/node/node.rs
@@ -2676,8 +2676,11 @@ impl Node {
             }),
         );
 
-        parent_document.remove_script_and_layout_blocker(cx);
+        // The post-connection steps can run script in any realm (an inserted iframe fires `load`
+        // synchronously, possibly at a listener from the node's old document), so the document
+        // that holds them must be the last one released.
         from_document.remove_script_and_layout_blocker(cx);
+        parent_document.remove_script_and_layout_blocker(cx);
     }
 
     /// <https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-replace-all>
